  "id": "Compound::DB01288 - Gene::155",
  "verbalization": "Fenoterol, a selective beta-2 adrenergic receptor agonist, is shown to bind to Adrb1 and Adrb2, both of which participate in the Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity pathway, which in turn is linked to Adrb3. This suggests that Fenoterol may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving the activation of beta-adrenergic receptors, ultimately leading to the activation of Adrb3. The high scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Fenoterol and Adrb3, with the binding of Fenoterol to Adrb1 and Adrb2 being the primary point of interaction. The shared pathway to Adrb3 implies that the activation of these receptors may converge on Adrb3, potentially influencing its function in a cellular context. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Fenoterol and Adrb3, though the exact downstream effects of Adrb3 activation remain to be fully elucidated.",
